⚡🇮🇶 Iraqi Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi reportedly told three Kurdish parliamentary blocs that the Kurdistan Regional Government (KRG) must comply with Baghdad’s decisions and permit the deployment of federal forces across the Kurdistan Region, according to a source who attended the meeting and spoke to Rudaw.

Al-Zaidi reportedly warned that failure to comply could prompt Baghdad to retake oil fields in disputed territories by force, construct a wall separating the Kurdistan Region from the rest of Iraq, and suspend all salary payments and financial transfers to the region.

